{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>כולנה</b> — Two times in the Masorah: here and the other: ואת עלית על כולנה. To teach that his grief over Benjamin surpassed all the grief he suffered over Simeon and Joseph, because he was confirmed in it three times. And we say: an infant — even though there is no divination, there is a sign. Another interpretation: כלנה is written defective, for upon him fell the food of their wives, who are his daughters-in-law."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:15.428434437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}